Work in $x = \ln S$ on $M + 1$ equally spaced nodes from $\ln S_0 - 5\sigma\sqrt T$ to $\ln S_0 + 5\sigma\sqrt T$, with $
u = r - 	frac12\sigma^2$. Take $N$ steps of $\Delta	au = T/N$ from the payoff, each setting $V_j \leftarrow a V_{j-1} + bV_j + cV_{j+1}$ at every inner node from the old values. Here $a = \Delta	au ig(	frac{\sigma^2}{2\Delta x^2} - 	frac{
u}{2\Delta x} ig)$, $b = 1 - \Delta	au ig(	frac{\sigma^2}{\Delta x^2} + r ig)$ and $c = \Delta	au ig(	frac{\sigma^2}{2\Delta x^2} + 	frac{
u}{2\Delta x} ig)$. Then set $V_0 = 0$ and $V_M = e^{x_M} - Ke^{-r	au}$. Return the middle node, where $x = \ln S_0$.

